            <div class="post-body__section reveal">
              <h2>What Is Trim Carpentry?</h2>
              <p>Trim carpentry focuses on the finishing touches of a home's interior, but in 2026, it's about more than aesthetics. It includes molding, baseboards, window and door casings, wainscoting, and other decorative elements that add architectural detail. Skilled trim carpenters ensure that each piece is precisely measured, cut, and installed for a seamless and polished look. These small details contribute to the overall harmony of your home's design, tying together different elements for a cohesive aesthetic.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="post-body__section reveal">
              <h2>The Importance of Quality Trim Work</h2>
              <p>Well-installed trim work not only enhances a home's aesthetics but also increases its value. Home renovation services often recommend trim upgrades as part of whole house renovations or custom home renovations. High-quality materials and expert craftsmanship ensure long-lasting beauty and durability.</p>
              <p>Beyond aesthetics, trim work serves a practical purpose. Baseboards protect walls from scuff marks and damage, while door and window casings help insulate against drafts. Investing in premium trim work can help improve the energy efficiency and longevity of your home's interior.</p>
            </div>

